CHAPTER II
WOMEN'S RIGHTS
Article 5
(1) Every woman has the right to: a. live and maintain her life;
live and improve the standard b. fulfill.
-6-
b. fulfill her basic needs to grow and develop properly, have a family, and continue her lineage;
c. develop her personality, to obtain education, and improve her quality of life in order to become a human being who is faithful, pious, responsible, of noble character, happy, and prosperous in accordance with Human Rights;
d. obtain justice, a sense of security, and freedom to express opinions without Discrimination;
e. be involved in every stage of the development process;
f. be free from slavery or enslavement and threats;
g. obtain protection of her person, Family, honor, dignity and property rights;
h. obtain welfare and a decent life; i. participate in politics;
j. perform legal acts;
k. be free to choose a partner in her marriage; and
l. obtain special protection in the implementation of her work or profession against matters that may threaten her safety and or health in relation to women's reproductive function.
(2) Every wife during the marriage bond has the same rights and responsibilities as her husband over all matters relating to her marital life, relations with her children, and ownership and management of joint property in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.
(3) After the dissolution of marriage, a woman has rights and responsibilities with her former husband over all matters relating to children with due regard to the best interests of the child.

